# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKA 96's TAIL AND PISKAOT 97-103 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 12 — CHAPTER 14, 2026-09-21; the one run, THE FIRST HALF): the children
# and the cuts (96:9-12), the holy people (97), the signs and the ra'ah (98), the abomination (99), the ten beasts (100), the beast fit to eat and the four
# exceptions (101-102), the birds (103) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation of the shelf CUT by consonants (ch14_ink.SP_ —
# a miss lands in FAIL, asserted empty by the ledger writer); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, the code checked before it is
# typed: I1 the a fortiori, I2 the analogy, I3 the paradigm). Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 13's form (ch13_rows_sifrei_82_86.py).
from ch14_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(96, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU ARE CHILDREN OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" (14:1) — R. JUDAH: IF YOU BEHAVE AS CHILDREN, YOU ARE CHILDREN; IF NOT, YOU ARE NOT. R. MEIR: EITHER WAY YOU ARE CHILDREN OF THE LORD YOUR GOD, AND SO IT SAYS "AND THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL SHALL BE …" (HOSEA 2:1). PISKA 96\'s TAIL, THE FIRST ROW ON THE CHAPTER — left by sitting 11 ({SP_(96, 9, "אם", "נוהגים", "אתם", "מנהג", "בנים")} "if you behave as children"; {SP_(96, 9, "בין", "כך", "ובין", "כך")} "either way"): THE SONSHIP CONDITIONAL OR UNCONDITIONAL — a two-arm reading of the chapter\'s first clause (the exam: Kiddushin 36a; the English\'s note Mishnah Avot 3:14) — THE INK: "you are children of the LORD" ONE seat in the Bible (computed); Exodus 4:22\'s "My son, My firstborn" the kin. Fresh.')
srow(96, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT CUT YOURSELVES" — DO NOT MAKE FACTIONS, BUT BE ALL ONE FACTION, AND SO IT SAYS "HE BUILDS HIS CHAMBERS IN THE HEAVENS AND HAS FOUNDED HIS BAND UPON THE EARTH" (AMOS 9:6). The row folded in by its consonants — Amos 9:6 alone in its brackets ({SP_(96, 10, "לא", "תעשו", "אגדות")} "do not make factions"; {SP_(96, 10, "היו", "כלכם", "אגדה", "אחת")} "be all one band"): THE VERB READ BY ITS LETTERS as "band" (the English\'s note on the assonance of two roots) — a second law drawn from the cutting\'s word: no factions in one court (the exam: Yevamot 13b-14a; Mishnah Avot 3:9 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(96, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOU SHALL NOT CUT YOURSELVES" — YOU SHALL NOT CUT YOURSELVES AS OTHERS CUT THEMSELVES, AS IT IS SAID "AND THEY CUT THEMSELVES AFTER THEIR MANNER" (1 KINGS 18:28). ({SP_(96, 11, "כדרך", "שאחרים", "מתגודדים")} "as others cut themselves"): THE PLAIN SENSE — the mourners\' cutting, Baal\'s prophets at Carmel the run\'s case; THE INK: the root\'s six seats in the Bible, the Torah\'s ONE here, 1 Kings 18:28 the narrative twin (computed). Fresh.')
srow(96, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOR MAKE A BALDNESS" — MIGHT THEY BE LIABLE ONLY FOR BETWEEN THE EYES? WHENCE THE WHOLE HEAD? "ON THEIR HEAD" (LEVITICUS 21:5). MIGHT THE PRIESTS, ON WHOM SCRIPTURE ADDED COMMANDMENTS, BE LIABLE FOR EACH BALDNESS AND FOR THE HEAD AS FOR BETWEEN THE EYES, BUT ISRAEL ONLY ONCE AND ONLY BETWEEN THE EYES? "BALDNESS", "BALDNESS" FOR AN ANALOGY — AS THE PRIESTS\', SO ISRAEL\'S; AND AS ISRAEL\'S ONLY FOR THE DEAD, SO THE PRIESTS\' ONLY FOR THE DEAD. ({SP_(96, 12, "קרחה", "קרחה", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "baldness, baldness, for an analogy"; {SP_(96, 12, "אין", "חיבים", "אלא", "על", "המת")} "liable only for the dead"): I2 (checked) ON THE TORAH\'S TWO SEATS OF THE WORD (computed) — THE ANALOGY RUNS BOTH WAYS: the priests\' verse gives Israel the whole head and the count, Israel\'s verse gives the priests the condition "for the dead" (the English\'s note Sifra Emor 1:1-3); the exam: Mishnah Makkot 3:5, Makkot 20a. Fresh.')
srow(97, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR YOU ARE A HOLY PEOPLE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" (14:2) — SANCTIFY YOURSELF. "FOR YOU ARE A HOLY PEOPLE" — THE HOLINESS THAT IS UPON YOU, IT CAUSED IT FOR YOU. The head row of piska 97 ({SP_(97, 1, "קדש", "את", "עצמך")} "sanctify yourself"; {SP_(97, 1, "קדשה", "שהיא", "עליך")} "the holiness that is upon you"): THE REASON CLAUSE READ AS A COMMAND AND AS A CAUSE — the holiness the ground of the cutting\'s bar; THE INK: "a holy people" THREE in the Bible (7:6, 14:2, 14:21), 14:2 IS 7:6 with the second "your God" dropped — 18 of 19 tokens in order (computed). Fresh.')
srow(97, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: DO NOT CAUSE ANOTHER PEOPLE TO BE HOLY LIKE YOU. ({SP_(97, 2, "לא", "תגרם", "לעם", "אחר")} "do not cause another people"): the holiness not to be lent by imitation. Fresh.')
srow(97, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE LORD HAS CHOSEN YOU" — "FOR THE LORD HAS CHOSEN JACOB FOR HIMSELF" (PSALM 135:4); "TO BE HIS TREASURED PEOPLE" — "ISRAEL FOR HIS TREASURE" (PSALM 135:4). ({SP_(97, 3, "כי", "יעקב", "בחר", "לו", "יה")} "for the LORD has chosen Jacob"): the Psalm\'s two clauses laid on the verse\'s two (the English\'s note: a marginal insertion) — THE INK: "treasure" eight in the Bible, Psalm 135:4 among them (computed). Fresh.')
srow(97, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS CHOSEN YOU TO BE HIS TREASURED PEOPLE FROM ALL THE PEOPLES" — IT TEACHES THAT EACH AND EVERY ONE IS BELOVED BEFORE THE HOLY ONE MORE THAN ALL THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD. ({SP_(97, 4, "שכל", "אחד", "ואחד", "חביב")} "that each and every one is beloved"): THE SINGULAR "YOU" READ AS EACH ONE (the English\'s note) — the register\'s singular the datum; "beloved" the word Onkelos gives "treasure" (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(97, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN MORE THAN THE FIRST FATHERS? "FROM ALL THE PEOPLES THAT ARE ON THE FACE OF THE EARTH" — SAY NOW: MORE THAN THOSE BEFORE AND THOSE AFTER, BUT NOT MORE THAN THE FIRST FATHERS. ({SP_(97, 5, "ולא", "מאבות", "הראשונים")} "but not more than the first fathers"): THE CLAUSE\'S LIMIT — the peoples on the earth the comparison\'s set, the patriarchs outside it (7:7-8\'s love of the fathers the kin, read at chapter 7). Fresh.')
srow(98, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND EVERY BEAST THAT PARTS THE HOOF AND CLEAVES THE CLEFT INTO TWO HOOFS AND CHEWS THE CUD" (14:6) — UNLESS IT HAS THESE THREE SIGNS IT IS NOT PERMITTED FOR EATING. The head row of piska 98 — heading on 14:6 BEFORE piskaot 99-100 on 14:3-4 (the heads not in verse order, computed) ({SP_(98, 1, "עד", "שיהו", "בה", "שלשה", "סימנים")} "unless it has three signs"): THE SIGNS COUNTED THREE from the verse\'s three clauses — the parting, the cleaving into two, the cud — where Leviticus 11:3 has the same three without "two" (14:6 is 11:3 with "two hoofs" for "hoofs", asserted); the exam: Mishnah Chullin 3:6, Chullin 59a. Fresh.')
srow(98, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ABBA HANAN IN THE NAME OF R. ELIEZER: THE CLEFT ONE (THE SHESUAH) IS A KIND OF WILD BEAST. ({SP_(98, 2, "השסועה", "מין", "חיה")} "the cleft one is a kind of beast"): THE ONE WORD THIS CHAPTER ADDS TO LEVITICUS 11:4 READ AS A CREATURE\'S NAME — "the cleft one" ONE seat in the Bible (computed); the exam: Chullin 60b (the creature with two backs and two spines). Fresh.')
srow(98, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JOSIAH SAID: WHEREVER "BIRD" (TZIPPOR) IS SAID, SCRIPTURE SPEAKS OF A CLEAN ONE (14:11). ({SP_(98, 3, "כל", "מקום", "שנאמר", "צפור")} "wherever bird is said"): THE NOUN\'S SENSE FIXED FOR THE WHOLE TORAH from 14:11\'s "every clean bird" — the rule 228:5 applies to the bird\'s nest (the outside row); THE INK: "bird" the chapter\'s one token (computed). Fresh.')
srow(98, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ISAAC SAID: A CLEAN FOWL IS CALLED "FOWL" AND IS CALLED "BIRD"; THE UNCLEAN IS CALLED ONLY "FOWL". The row without a citation ({SP_(98, 4, "עוף", "טהור", "נקרא", "עוף", "ונקרא", "צפור")} "a clean fowl is called fowl and called bird"): THE TWO NOUNS OF THE LIST\'S TWO FRAMES — "every clean bird" (14:11) before, "every clean fowl" (14:20) after — read as a lexicon (the English\'s note Sifra Shemini 5:3). Fresh.')
srow(98, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE RA\'AH" (14:13) — THIS IS THE DAYYAH, AND ALL OF THEM ARE A KIND OF DAYYAH. ISSI SON OF JUDAH: THERE ARE A HUNDRED KINDS OF FOWL IN THE EAST, AND ALL OF THEM ARE A KIND OF AYYAH. ({SP_(98, 5, "והראה", "זו", "דיה")} "the ra\'ah — this is the dayyah"; {SP_(98, 5, "מאה", "מיני", "עופות", "במזרח")} "a hundred kinds of fowl in the East"): THE THREE NAMES OF 14:13 ONE BIRD BY ITS KINDS — the ra\'ah the dayyah, the dayyah the ayyah; the hundred a count with no play (the exam: Chullin 63b). Fresh.')
srow(98, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'AYYAH, DAYYAH, RA\'AH, DA\'AH — WHY WERE THEY REPEATED IN THE REPETITION OF THE TORAH? IN THE BEAST BECAUSE OF THE CLEFT ONE, AND IN THE FOWL BECAUSE OF THE DAYYAH. ({SP_(98, 6, "למה", "נשנו", "במשנה", "תורה")} "why were they repeated in the Repetition of the Torah"; {SP_(98, 6, "בבהמה", "מפני", "השסועה")} "in the beast because of the cleft one"): THE REASON THE TWIN CHAPTER EXISTS, BY THE SHELF — the two names this chapter adds (the shesuah at 14:7, the dayyah at 14:13) are the whole gain of the restatement; THE INK: the ra\'ah\'s resh for Leviticus 11:14\'s dalet, 14:13\'s three names against 11:14\'s two (asserted); the English\'s note on the rows\' order and attestation stands as the export\'s. Fresh.')
srow(99, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT EAT ANY ABOMINATION" (14:3) — R. ELIEZER: WHENCE THAT ONE WHO SLITS THE EAR OF A FIRSTLING AND EATS OF IT TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION? "YOU SHALL NOT EAT ANY ABOMINATION." The head row of piska 99 ({SP_(99, 1, "לצורם", "אזן", "הבכור")} "one who slits the ear of a firstling"): THE ABOMINATION READ AS A THING MADE ABHORRENT BY A DEED — the maimed firstling (the English\'s note on the rule); the exam: Bekhorot 34a-35a. Fresh.')
srow(99, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'OTHERS SAY: OF DISQUALIFIED CONSECRATED ANIMALS SCRIPTURE SPEAKS — "ABOMINATION" IS SAID HERE AND "ABOMINATION" IS SAID THERE, "YOU SHALL NOT SACRIFICE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD AN OX OR A SHEEP … FOR IT IS AN ABOMINATION TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" (17:1): AS THERE THE DISQUALIFIED CONSECRATED, SO HERE. ({SP_(99, 2, "נאמר", "כאן", "תועבה", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "abomination is said here and said there"): I2 (checked) on the chapter\'s one "abomination" and 17:1\'s (computed: the book\'s seventeen, "abomination to the LORD your God" five) — NEVER READ AHEAD: 17:1 waits for its sitting, the analogy recorded here from its seat. Fresh.')
srow(100, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THIS IS THE BEAST WHICH YOU SHALL EAT: THE OX, THE SHEEP, THE GOAT; THE HART, THE GAZELLE, THE ROEBUCK" (14:4-5) — IT TEACHES THAT THE WILD BEAST IS INCLUDED IN "BEAST". The head row of piska 100 ({SP_(100, 1, "שחיה", "בכלל", "בהמה")} "that the wild beast is included in beast"): THE LIST\'S HEADER NOUN WIDENED BY ITS OWN LIST — the seven wild under "beast"; THE INK: the ten names here and not in Leviticus 11 (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(100, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT THE BEAST IS INCLUDED IN "WILD BEAST"? "THIS IS THE WILD BEAST …" (LEVITICUS 11:2). IT TEACHES THAT THE WILD BEAST IS CALLED BEAST AND THE BEAST WILD BEAST, AND THAT THE UNCLEAN BEASTS OUTNUMBER THE CLEAN — EVERYWHERE SCRIPTURE SPECIFIES THE FEWER. ({SP_(100, 2, "הכתוב", "פורט", "את", "המועט")} "Scripture specifies the fewer"): THE TWO HEADERS READ INTO EACH OTHER (11:2\'s "living thing" and 14:4\'s "beast" — the twin chapter\'s two nouns one class), and A COUNTING RULE — the list names the smaller set (103:7 says it of the birds). Fresh.')
srow(100, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE ANTELOPE" — R. YOSE: THE ANTELOPE IS THE WILD OX. The row without a citation ({SP_(100, 3, "תאו", "זה", "שור", "הבר")} "the antelope is the wild ox"): a name identified (the English\'s note Tosefta Kilayim 1:9; the exam: Chullin 80a). Fresh.')
srow(101, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND EVERY BEAST THAT PARTS THE HOOF" (14:6) — SINCE WE FIND THAT SCRIPTURE INCLUDED THE TORN LIKE THE TORN, I MIGHT INCLUDE THE DISQUALIFIED LIKE THE DISQUALIFIED — WHICH? THE ONE THAT PLOWED WITH AN OX AND AN ASS, AND CONSECRATED ANIMALS. "THE OX, THE SHEEP, THE GOAT" YOU SHALL EAT. The head row of piska 101 — the third piska on 14:6 ({SP_(101, 1, "החורש", "בשור", "וחמור")} "the one that plowed with an ox and an ass"): THE LIST\'S NAMES AS A LICENSE — an animal disqualified for the altar by a deed is still food (the English\'s note on the difficult text stands as the export\'s). Fresh.')
srow(101, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'I INCLUDE THESE, BUT NOT YET THE ONE THAT MOUNTED OR WAS MOUNTED, THE SET-ASIDE AND THE WORSHIPPED, THE HIRE AND THE PRICE, THE MIXED-BRED, THE TORN AND THE ONE BORN BY THE SIDE (MISHNAH TEMURAH 6:1)? "THE OX, THE SHEEP, THE GOAT …". ({SP_(101, 2, "הרובע", "ואת", "הנרבע")} "the one that mounted and the one mounted"; {SP_(101, 2, "וכלאים", "וטרפה", "ויוצא", "דופן")} "the mixed-bred, the torn and the one born by the side"): THE ALTAR\'S DISQUALIFICATIONS LISTED (the Mishnah\'s row cited in the Hebrew itself) AND EACH LICENSED AS FOOD BY THE NAMES — the English\'s note: the idolatry cases excepted by the Mishnah\'s own text. Fresh.')
srow(101, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'I INCLUDE THESE, BUT NOT YET THE ONE WITH WHICH A TRANSGRESSION WAS DONE BY ONE WITNESS OR BY THE OWNERS? "THE OX, THE SHEEP, THE GOAT." ({SP_(101, 3, "על", "פי", "עד", "אחד")} "by one witness"): the goring ox unconvicted still food. Fresh.')
srow(101, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'I INCLUDE THESE, BUT NOT YET THE ONE WITH WHICH A TRANSGRESSION WAS DONE BY TWO WITNESSES AND ITS SENTENCE NOT YET FINISHED? "THE OX, THE SHEEP, THE GOAT YOU SHALL EAT." ({SP_(101, 4, "ועדין", "לא", "נגמר", "דינו")} "and its sentence not yet finished"): the ox before its verdict still food (Exodus 21:28\'s stoned ox the kin, read at its sitting). Fresh.')
srow(101, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'I INCLUDE THESE THAT GREW IN CLEANNESS, BUT NOT YET THE OFFSPRING OF A FIT ONE THAT NURSED FROM A TORN ONE? "AMONG THE BEASTS." ({SP_(101, 5, "ולד", "כשרה", "שינקה", "מן", "הטרפה")} "the offspring of a fit one that nursed from a torn one"): the nursing no bar. Fresh.')
srow(101, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'I INCLUDE THE OFFSPRING OF A FIT ONE THAT NURSED FROM A TORN ONE, BUT NOT YET THE OFFSPRING OF A TORN ONE THAT NURSED FROM A CLEAN BEAST WITH AN UNCLEAN? "AMONG THE BEASTS" — EVERY BEAST. ({SP_(101, 6, "בבהמה", "כל", "הבהמה")} "among the beasts — every beast"): the phrase\'s generality the license. Fresh.')
srow(101, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AMONG THE BEASTS YOU SHALL EAT" — TO INCLUDE THE AFTERBIRTH. ({SP_(101, 7, "לרבות", "שליה")} "to include the afterbirth"): THE PREPOSITION\'S "IN" READ AS WHAT IS INSIDE THE BEAST — the exam: Chullin 68a-69a, 77a. Fresh.')
srow(101, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN IF PART OF IT CAME OUT? "IT." ({SP_(101, 8, "יצאת", "מקצתה")} "part of it came out"): the pronoun "it" (14:6) the limit — the whole born. Fresh.')
srow(101, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"IT YOU SHALL EAT" — IT FOR EATING, AND NO UNCLEAN BEAST FOR EATING. I HAVE ONLY A POSITIVE COMMAND; WHENCE A PROHIBITION TOO? "THE CAMEL, THE HARE, THE ROCK-BADGER AND THE SWINE" (14:7-8). ({SP_(101, 9, "אותה", "באכילה", "ואין", "בהמה", "טמאה", "באכילה")} "it for eating, and no unclean beast for eating"): THE POSITIVE COMMAND\'S IMPLIED NEGATIVE, THEN THE WRITTEN PROHIBITION — the four names the prohibition\'s seat (the English\'s note Sifra Shemini 3:1). Fresh.')
srow(101, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF THEIR FLESH YOU SHALL NOT EAT" — I HAVE ONLY THESE; THE REST OF THE UNCLEAN BEASTS WHENCE? IT IS A REASONING: IF THESE, WHICH HAVE SIGNS OF CLEANNESS, ARE UNDER A PROHIBITION, THE REST, WHICH HAVE NO SIGNS OF CLEANNESS — IS IT NOT REASONABLE THAT THEY BE UNDER A PROHIBITION FOR THEIR EATING? SO THE CAMEL, THE HARE, THE ROCK-BADGER AND THE SWINE ARE FROM SCRIPTURE, AND THE REST FROM AN A FORTIORI; THEIR POSITIVE COMMAND FROM SCRIPTURE, THEIR PROHIBITION FROM AN A FORTIORI. ({SP_(101, 10, "נמצאו", "הגמל", "והארנבת", "והשפן", "והחזיר", "מן", "הכתוב")} "so the camel, the hare, the rock-badger and the swine are from Scripture"; {SP_(101, 10, "מקל", "וחומר")} "from an a fortiori"): I1 (checked) — THE FOUR NAMED ARE THE CODE\'S CASES, THE REST DERIVED: the compile\'s rule that the written list is the exception set and the sign the class (the exam: Chullin 66b). Fresh.')
srow(102, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT THIS YOU SHALL NOT EAT … THE CLEFT ONE" (14:7) — R. AKIVA SAID: WAS MOSES A HUNTER OR AN ARCHER? RATHER, FROM HERE IS THE ANSWER TO THOSE WHO SAY THE TORAH IS NOT FROM HEAVEN. The one-row piska ({SP_(102, 1, "וכי", "משה", "קניגי", "היה")} "was Moses a hunter"; {SP_(102, 1, "אין", "תורה", "מן", "השמים")} "the Torah is not from Heaven"): THE FOUR EXCEPTIONS AS THE PROOF OF THE PROGRAM\'S AUTHOR — the closed list of the sign-holders (the exam: Chullin 60b). Fresh.')
srow(103, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY CLEAN BIRD YOU MAY EAT" (14:11) — SINCE IT IS SAID "THE PRIEST SHALL COMMAND AND TAKE FOR THE ONE BEING CLEANSED TWO LIVE CLEAN BIRDS" (LEVITICUS 14:4), MIGHT THE SENT ONE BE FORBIDDEN AS THE SLAUGHTERED ONE IS? "EVERY CLEAN BIRD YOU MAY EAT." The head row of piska 103 ({SP_(103, 1, "כשם", "ששחוטה", "אסורה", "כך", "משלחת", "אסורה")} "as the slaughtered one is forbidden so the sent one"): THE LEPER\'S TWO BIRDS BY CALL (Leviticus 14 read at its sitting) — the permission\'s clause released the bird set free. Fresh.')
srow(103, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'OR AS THE SENT ONE IS PERMITTED, SO THE SLAUGHTERED ONE PERMITTED? "AND THIS IS WHAT YOU SHALL NOT EAT OF THEM" (14:12). ({SP_(103, 2, "כשם", "שמשלחת", "מתרת", "כך", "שחוטה")} "as the sent one is permitted so the slaughtered one"): THE TWO FRAMES ARGUE BOTH DIRECTIONS — the permission (14:11) frees the sent bird, the prohibition\'s header (14:12) holds the slaughtered one; the English\'s note: a reworking of Sifra Metzora 1:12. Fresh.')
srow(103, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE EAGLE, THE OSSIFRAGE, THE OSPREY" — R. AKIVA: "EAGLE" IS SAID HERE AND "EAGLE" IS SAID THERE (LEVITICUS 11:13); AS THERE ALL NAMED WITH THE EAGLE ARE UNDER "DO NOT FEED" AND "DO NOT EAT", SO HERE. ({SP_(103, 3, "נאמר", "כאן", "נשר", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "eagle is said here and eagle is said there"; {SP_(103, 3, "בבל", "תאכיל", "ובבל", "תאכל")} "under do not feed and do not eat"): I2 (checked) ON THE LIST\'S FIRST NAME — the whole list carried by its head from the twin chapter, two prohibitions (feeding and eating) on each name (the exam: Chullin 63b-64a). Fresh.')
srow(103, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: "AYYAH" IS SAID HERE (14:13) AND "AYYAH" IS SAID THERE (LEVITICUS 11:14); AS HERE THE AYYAH MADE THE RA\'AH A KIND OF AYYAH, SO THERE. ({SP_(103, 4, "עשה", "את", "הראה", "מין", "איה")} "made the ra\'ah a kind of ayyah"): I2 (checked) ON THE SECOND NAME — the ra\'ah, absent from Leviticus 11 by its letters (asserted), read into it as a kind; 98:5-6\'s identification by the analogy\'s road. Fresh.')
srow(103, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"RAVEN" (14:14) — THIS IS THE GREAT RAVEN; "AND EVERY RAVEN" — TO INCLUDE THE VALLEY RAVEN AND THE RAVEN THAT COMES AT THE HEAD OF DOVES; "AFTER ITS KIND" — TO INCLUDE THE STARLING. ({SP_(103, 5, "להביא", "את", "הזרזיר")} "to include the starling"): each particle a kind (the English\'s note Sifra Shemini 5:4); the exam: Chullin 65a. Fresh.')
srow(103, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'["THE HAWK" — THIS IS THE HAWK;] WHEN IT SAYS "AFTER ITS KIND" (14:15) — TO INCLUDE THE BEN HORIYAH. ({SP_(103, 6, "להביא", "את", "בן", "הוריה")} "to include the ben horiyah"): the bracketed clause the editor\'s (the English\'s note on the name\'s versions). Fresh.')
srow(103, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE OSTRICH … AND THE LITTLE OWL … AND THE PELICAN, THE CARRION-VULTURE AND THE CORMORANT" (14:15-17) — IT TEACHES THAT THE CLEAN FOWL OUTNUMBER THE UNCLEAN; EVERYWHERE SCRIPTURE SPECIFIES THE FEWER. ({SP_(103, 7, "שעוף", "טהור", "מרבה", "מעוף", "טמא")} "that the clean fowl outnumber the unclean"): THE COUNTING RULE AGAIN (100:2 of the beasts) — the unclean listed by name because fewer, the clean by a frame because many; THE INK: twenty-one names against Leviticus 11:13-19\'s twenty (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(103, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'(MISHNAH CHULLIN 3:6) THE SIGNS OF THE BEAST AND THE WILD BEAST WERE SAID FROM THE TORAH; THE SIGNS OF THE FOWL WERE NOT SAID. THE SAGES SAID: EVERY FOWL THAT SEIZES IS UNCLEAN, AS IT SAYS "THE EAGLE" — AS THE EAGLE, WHICH HAS NO CROP, NO EXTRA TOE, NO PEELABLE GIZZARD, AND SEIZES AND EATS, IS UNCLEAN, SO EVERYTHING LIKE IT IS FORBIDDEN; WHAT IS NOT LIKE IT, PERMITTED. The row citing the Mishnah in its own Hebrew ({SP_(103, 8, "סימני", "העוף", "לא", "נאמרו")} "the signs of the fowl were not said"; {SP_(103, 8, "כל", "עוף", "דורס", "טמא")} "every fowl that seizes is unclean"): I3 (checked) — THE PERMITTED BIRDS HAVE NO SIGN IN THE INK (asserted: the two frames and the names alone), THE SIGNS BUILT FROM THE EAGLE AS THE FATHER — the compile\'s parameter the_birds_signs from the answer sheet, not the code (the code/data separation law\'s own case; Mishnah Chullin 3:6 the row\'s citation, routed to 12b\'s docket). Fresh.')
srow(103, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY CLEAN FOWL YOU MAY EAT" (14:20) — A POSITIVE COMMAND. ({SP_(103, 9, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive command"): the second frame read as the prescription (101:9\'s form for the beasts). Fresh.')
